      {
        "id": 131332,
        "name": "MrLeRobot",
        "username": "MrLeRobot",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mrlerobot/{size}/1932_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-02-13T07:25:33.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"McBehrer\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mcbehrer/48/1850_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> McBehrer:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>MrLeRobot wrote:</b><br><blockquote>Progeny's \"Hour of Reckoning\":Progeny beating Legacy while Dark Visionnary and Nightmist are there, just watching... Ok, so Progeny is most definitely evil. It is hinted that Dark Visionnary is kinda evil too. Considering the last few points noted earlier, what if Dark Visionnary and Nighmist BOTH betrayed the heroes!? Dark Visionnary is known to be exorcised from her dark passenger at some point, but what about Nightmist? Maybe she played with too much eldritch magic... Perhaps we'll see Nightmist in Tactics, but on the villain side?The title of the card would actually make a lot of sense looking at it that way, at least for me...\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nI don't know... judging from the flavor text, she just can't reform because it is unsafe. Now, Dark Visionary may be evil at that point (odd, considering she is still a playable hero) but she doesn't seem like she is.I mean, MAYBE, but I don't know... Then again, if that means she'll be playable in Tactics, then I guess I can survive...\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Maybe she can't reform because she used too much of her powers during a fight (against other heroes maybe?) wich consumed part of her mist body and now, if she tries to reform, she might not be complete and that would be dangerous for her…? Speculation, of course…</p>",
