      {
        "id": 131334,
        "name": "TheSoundOfTrees",
        "username": "TheSoundOfTrees",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/t/da6949/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2015-02-13T10:17:57.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Nielzabub\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/nielzabub/48/1986_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Nielzabub:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>TheSoundOfTrees wrote:</b><br><blockquote>Yes, MrLeRobot, I think that a \"Voss after his exile\", coming back as some kind of \"demon\" , or with a new army of mystical creatures he built during exile, seem a good candidate for a new villain. Unless he already is the zombie body of Gloomweaver II :)\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nThe only problem with that theory is that Voss's deck would be the same, so the minions would still be minions and they would still be aliens unless Voss's cards had text that made that otherwise. I like the idea of Voss coming back all mystical though, that might be neat.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I was thinking of a new deck - a new villain, with its own deck, but with the background of being what Voss has become, not a simple promo card.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><a class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/mrlerobot\">@MrLeRobot</a> : It was a joke ! I don't think Gloomy has taken Voss's body, nor did I see any clue that it could be true. But, well, it seems like something that could happen in a super-hero comic book. I think I remember having read somewhere that it was Spite's body, but I may be wrong.</p>\n<p>I think that your idea of Voss getting back from the Realm with a new villain deck would be even more comic-bookish - and far more interesting. Any way, the question of what happens with Voss, and later Nightmist, is one of the big unanswered misteries of SotM, with the origins of Dark Watch and the \"rebirth\" of Mr Fixer, in my opinion.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
