      {
        "id": 131338,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-02-13T15:02:47.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>So likelihood of a new promo: &nbsp;Phantaskippy's top 5.</p><p>1. &nbsp;Apostate: &nbsp;His deck works so well and his Character card is so easy to change up, and his storyline has to be a thing that continues.</p><p>2. &nbsp;Voss: &nbsp;I just can't imagine Wrath having two Thorathian decks not somehow leading to a revival of the army, plus with that engine the character card could go anywhere.</p><p><span>3. &nbsp;Dreamer: &nbsp;Would really work well. &nbsp;We know she's still around, and the possibility that Visionary alters her own timeline substantially after the \"Fixed Point\" could lead to all kinds of fun. &nbsp;As a minion heavy deck there could be all kinds of difference.</span></p><p>4. &nbsp;Kismet: &nbsp;Less for storyline and later importance, more off deck mechanics, her deck could be very different with a promo.</p><p><span>5. &nbsp;Wager Master: &nbsp;I thought it in playtesting and still do, this deck seems set up for a promo. &nbsp;Or maybe I'm crazy. &nbsp;I also don't see one coming with the last expansion. &nbsp;I could see him ending up a servant of the big bad after finally being defeated. &nbsp;It could be wierd.</span></p><div>&nbsp;</div><p>I don't see Akash or Matriarch Happening, largely because their character cards are so heavily invested in the engine that makes them run. &nbsp;There isn't a lot of room to redirect that engine to another purpose.</p>",
